{"s":[[null,1,[["p",["The Grape is a ",["l","水果","fruit"]," that is both a ",["l","采集","forageable"]," item and a standard ",["l","农作物","crop"],":"]],["l",0,[[1,["In ",["l","夏季","Summer"],", Grapes are a ",["l","采集","forageable"]," fruit found that grows wild throughout Stardew Valley or can be grown from ",["l","夏季种子","Summer Seeds"],". Specifically, forageable Grapes can be found at: the ",["l","边远森林","Backwoods"]," (62% of all forageable items at this location); ",["l","深山","the Mountain"]," (62%); the ",["l","巴士站","Bus Stop"]," (27%); the ",["l","铁路","Railroad"]," (27%); or, the ",["l","农场地图","Forest Farm Map"]," (25%). It can also randomly be found in ",["l","垃圾桶","Garbage Can"],"s during Summer."]],[1,["In ",["l","秋季","Fall"],", Grapes are a standard crop that takes ten days to grow from a ",["l","葡萄种子","Grape Starter"]," to maturity; the plants can be re-harvested every three days."]]]],["p",["Grapes grown as a crop (in Fall) receive the +10% ",["l","技能","Tiller"]," profession bonus when sold (as do all crops). However, foraged Grapes in summer do not get the Tiller bonus. If you combine Summer and Fall grapes into the same stack, the entire stack will receive the Tiller bonus (see ",["l","水果","the Fruit page"]," for more details)."]],["p",["Other than the Tiller profession bonus, foraged Grapes and crop-grown Grapes are identical and can be used interchangeably in crafting, gifts, bundles, recipes, and quests."]]]],["Stages",2,[["p",["You cannot walk through grape plants grown from a Grape Starter at any stage of growth. You can walk through dead Grape plants."]],["t",[[{"h":1,"v":["Stage 1"]},{"h":1,"v":["Stage 2"]},{"h":1,"v":["Stage 3"]},{"h":1,"v":["Stage 4"]},{"h":1,"v":["Stage 5"]},{"h":1,"v":["Harvest"]},{"h":1,"v":["After-Harvest"]}],[[["f","Grape_Stage_1.png",48]],[["f","Grape_Stage_2.png",48]],[["f","Grape_Stage_3.png",48]],[["f","Grape_Stage_4.png",48]],[["f","Grape_Stage_5.png",48]],[["f","Grape_Stage_6.png",48]],[["f","Grape_Stage_7.png",48]]],[